## Problem

`POST /api/specialists`, `PUT /api/specialists/:id` and `DELETE /api/specialists/:id` forwarded the store's plain `Error`s with no mapping, so four client mistakes came out as `500 {"error":"Internal server error"}`:

- a taken name (`Specialist name already exists`);
- an unknown id on `PUT` or `DELETE` (`Specialist not found`);
- editing a built-in Specialist (its read-only message).

The settings pane prints the server's message verbatim, so the user got the generic text while the store already knew the reason. The neighbouring MCP-server surface answers `400` for its conflict and `404` for its missing id, so the Specialist routes were the outlier.

## Change

One guard around the three Specialist routes, keyed on the store's own rejection wording (the same shape `services/api/src/http/custom-mcp.ts` already uses):

- `Specialist not found` → `404`, message unchanged;
- every other rejection the store raises for these routes → `400`, message unchanged (pinned by name in the test: required/limits, taken name, unavailable skills/connectors, built-in read-only, built-in delete, referenced-by-session, `enabled` type);
- anything else is rethrown to the catch-all, so a genuine fault is still `500` and still reaches the `unclassified_request_error` log rather than being relabelled `400`.

No store message, no validation rule and no client code changed.

## Verification

- `node --import tsx --test src/specialists-http.test.ts` (from `services/api`) — 10 tests, 10 pass, against a real `createApiServer` on a temp data dir:
  - duplicate name `400` with `Specialist name already exists`; first create still `201`;
  - unknown id `404` on `PUT` and on `DELETE`;
  - built-in edit `400` with its read-only message; `PUT {"enabled":false}` still `200` and persists; built-in delete still `400`;
  - an injected unexpected fault inside the block still answers `500 "Internal server error"`;
  - the guard's negatives: `Catalog database is not initialized`, a `TypeError`, `ENOTDIR`, and messages that merely contain "must"/"cannot"/"invalid" stay faults.
- `pnpm --filter @sciencediscovery/api typecheck` — clean.

Fixes #935
